          %h2#references References
          %p
            Brauer groups are named after
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Brauer"} Richard Brauer
          %p Original discussion includes
          %ul
            %li#Grothendieck64
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"}> Alexander Grothendieck
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Le groupe de Brauer: II. Théories cohomologiques
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=SB_1964-1966__9__287_0"} Numdam
            %li#Grothendieck68
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandre+Grothendieck"}> Alexandre Grothendieck
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Le groupe de Brauer
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dix exposés sur la cohomologie des schémas
          %p An introduction is in
          %ul
            %li
              Pete Clark,
              %em On the Brauer group
              (2003) (
              %a{:href => "http://math.uga.edu/~pete/trivial2003.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Duskin"}> John Duskin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Azumaya complex of a commutative ring
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 1348
            %li#Street
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Descent
                = succeed ")" do
                  %em Brauer groups
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.mq.edu.au/~street/Descent.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Some combinatorial aspects of descent theory
                %strong 12
                (2004) 537-576,
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0303175"} math.CT/0303175
                (sec. 12,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %em Brauer groups
          %p
            The relation to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+cohomology"} etale cohomology
            is discussed in
          %ul#Milne
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Milne"}> James Milne
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Étale cohomology
          %ul#Giraud
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Giraud"}> Jean Giraud
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Cohomologie non abelienne
          %ul#deJong
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ofer+Gabber"}> Ofer Gabber
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Some theorems on Azumaya algebras
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aise+Johan+de+Jong"}> Aise Johan de Jong
                ,
                %em A result of Gabber
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.columbia.edu/~dejong/papers/2-gabber.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %ul#Bertuccioni
            %li
              Inta Bertuccioni,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Brauer groups and cohomology
          %p
            Brauer groups of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superalgebras"} superalgebras
            are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C.+T.+C.+Wall"}> C. T. C. Wall
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Graded Brauer groups
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
                ,
                %em Notes on spinors
                in
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Fields+and+Strings"} Quantum Fields and Strings
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Donovan"}> Peter Donovan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Karoubi"} Max Karoubi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Graded Brauer groups and K-theory with local coefficients
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.jussieu.fr/~karoubi/Donavan.K.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Refinement to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brauer+%E2%88%9E-groups"} Brauer ∞-groups
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Szymik11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markus+Szymik"}> Markus Szymik
                ,
                %em Brauer spaces for commutative rings and structured ring spectra
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1110.2956"}> arXiv:1110.2956
                )
            %li#BakerRichterSzymik12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Baker"}> Andrew Baker
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Birgit+Richter"} Birgit Richter
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markus+Szymik"} Markus Szymik
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Brauer groups for commutative
                    = succeed "-algebras" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝕊
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1005.5370"} arXiv:1005.5370
          %p
            Unification of all this in a theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2Cn%29-modules"} (infinity,n)-modules
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Haugseng14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rune+Haugseng"}> Rune Haugseng
              ,
              %em
                The higher Morita category of
                = succeed "-algebras" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_n
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1412.8459"}> arXiv:1412.8459
              )
          %p The “bigger Brauer group” is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Taylor82
              %p
                J. Taylor,
                %em A bigger Brauer group
                Pacific J. Math. 103 (1982), 163-203 (
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.pjm/1102724219"}> projecteuclid
                )
            %li#CaenepeelGrandjean98
              %p
                S. Caenepeel, F. Grandjean,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em A note on Taylor’s Brauer group
            %li#HeinlothSchoeer08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jochen+Heinloth"}> Jochen Heinloth
                , Stefan Schröer,
                %em The bigger Brauer group and twisted sheaves
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0803.3563"}> arXiv:0803.3563
                )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jochen+Heinloth"}> Jochen Heinloth
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Levine"} Marc Levine
              = succeed "," do
                %em Forschungsseminar: Brauer groups and Artin stack
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.uni-due.de/~mat903/sem/brauer.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The observation that passing to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
            makes also the non-torsion elements in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi et
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^2_{et}(-,\mathbb{G}_m)
            be represented by (derived)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Azumaya+algebras"} Azumaya algebras
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Toen10
